cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SocialMemBench in academic work, please cite this benchmark."
title: "SocialMemBench: Evaluating AI Memory Architectures in Social Group Conversations"
abstract: >-
  SocialMemBench is the first benchmark that evaluates external memory systems
  (the write/index/retrieve substrate between sessions) in social group settings
  with 3+ co-present speakers. It comprises 43 ego networks, 1,031 question-answer
  pairs across 9 query types, and evaluation results across 8+ memory-system
  conditions including Mem0, LangMem, Cognee, and Graphiti.
